<title>GERMANY: Yen downward correction fully completed - MOF source.</title>
<headline>Yen downward correction fully completed - MOF source.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yen's downward correction has been completed, a senior official at Japan's Ministry of Finance said on Saturday.</p>
<p>A Japanese delegation was in Berlin to meet with other members of the so-called Group of Seven (G7) of the world's most industrialised nations.</p>
<p>The yen has been hard hit by the dollar's recent strength, and Japanese officials have been known to fear a stronger dollar would lead Japan's trade surplus to balloon again and further damage stock prices.</p>
<p>The U.S. Germany, Japan, France, Italy, Canada and Britain are members of the G7.</p>
<p>--Yoshiko Mori, Berlin Newsroom, +49 30 2039810</p>
